volumebutton: say "No sound card found" when there is none

Without any sound card -- no driver running, as on a QNX system without
io-snd or a virtual machine without audio -- the button showed "Volume
control is not configured", which points at the settings dialog, where
nothing can be chosen. Tell that case apart (snd_card_next finds no card)
and say so; with a card but no element chosen the old text stays.

Upstream-Status: Pending

--- a/src/volumebutton.vala
+++ b/src/volumebutton.vala
@@ -88,7 +88,14 @@
                     tooltip_text = "%s: %d%s".printf(alsa.channel, (int) volume, "%");
                 }
             } else {
-                tooltip_text = _("Volume control is not configured");
+                // no card at all (no sound driver running) is not a setting
+                // the user can fix in the dialog: say so
+                int card = -1;
+                if (Alsa.Card.next(ref card) != 0 || card < 0) {
+                    tooltip_text = _("No sound card found");
+                } else {
+                    tooltip_text = _("Volume control is not configured");
+                }
             }
         }
 
